hip-flat-work-group-size: a fix to intel/llvm v7.2.0, applied by tools/intel_llvm_build.py.

A SYCL kernel's work-group size reaches NVIDIA's code as NVVM annotations (SYCLCreateNVVMAnnotationsPass), and AMD's
only from the reqd_work_group_size attribute (clang's AMDGPU code generation); the max_work_group_size attribute and
property and max_linear_work_group_size give it none: such an AMD kernel was compiled for work-groups of up to 1024
work-items, which on a wave64 GPU (gfx906) limits it to 64 VGPRs and spills the rest to scratch memory (2,298 of the
engine's 4,007 kernels on v7.1.1, which gave none of them), whatever size it is launched with.  The same pass now
gives an AMDGCN kernel the range as amdgpu-flat-work-group-size: N,N for reqd_work_group_size, 1,N for the others (N
the product of the dimensions, at most 1024; a kernel with its own amdgpu-flat-work-group-size, the attribute's
included, keeps it).
---
diff --git a/clang/lib/CodeGen/BackendUtil.cpp b/clang/lib/CodeGen/BackendUtil.cpp
index 6add0c5c43..ccfcffb9ca 100644
--- a/clang/lib/CodeGen/BackendUtil.cpp
+++ b/clang/lib/CodeGen/BackendUtil.cpp
@@ -1288,7 +1288,8 @@ void EmitAssemblyHelper::RunOptimizationPipeline(
       // and before cleaning up metadata)
       MPM.addPass(RecordSYCLAspectNamesPass());
 
-      if (TargetTriple.isNVPTX())
+      // NVPTX: the NVVM annotations; AMDGCN: the flat work-group size range
+      if (TargetTriple.isNVPTX() || TargetTriple.isAMDGCN())
         MPM.addPass(SYCLCreateNVVMAnnotationsPass());
 
       // Remove SYCL metadata added by the frontend, like sycl_aspects
